# An UNSET frame local passed as a call argument — ouroboros#132.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that this SEGFAULTED before #132, and nothing
# in the suite noticed. The borrowed call-argument read went through
# aot_getb_ic, whose documented contract is "env_get's NULL-on-miss" — it
# returns a C NULL pointer, not a null Value. Handed to a callee that
# dereferences it, that is a wild pointer:
#
#   VM       exit 1, "len: null has no length"
#   AOT pre  exit 139, Segmentation fault (core dumped)
#   AOT post exit 1, matching the VM
#
# `x` is bound only on the n > 0 branch, so `f of 0` reads it unset. That is
# ordinary EigenScript — `if` creates no scope and a read before the first
# assignment is a null, not an error — which is why the crash was reachable
# from plain code rather than a corner.
#
# Both sides must die with the same code and a normalized message. Verified to
# FAIL on the pre-#132 tree (rc 139 vs 1) and pass after, so it is a guard with
# a demonstrated fault class rather than a decoration.

define g(d) as:
    return (len of d)

define f(n) as:
    if n > 0:
        x is {"a": 1, "b": 2}
    return g of x

print of (f of 1)
print of (f of 0)
